# ############################################################################
# !!!  PLACEHOLDER OWNERS - CODE-OWNER REVIEW IS NOT ENFORCED YET  !!!
# Every @your-org/* team below is a placeholder. Until they are replaced with
# real teams, GitHub silently ignores these lines and NO code-owner review is
# required for any path (including IAM, KMS, org policy and CI).
# The "CODEOWNERS placeholders" job in terraform-plan.yml warns on every run;
# set the repository variable CODEOWNERS_ENFORCE=true after replacing them so
# a placeholder reappearing fails CI (docs/guides/CI_SECRETS.md).
# ############################################################################
#
# CODEOWNERS — team ownership for the landing zone (audit L / bus-factor).
#
# ACTION REQUIRED: replace every @your-org/* placeholder below with your real
# GitHub teams. This scaffold is INERT until all of the following are true:
#   1. The teams exist and each has at least one member.
#   2. Branch protection on the default branch has "Require review from Code
#      Owners" enabled (docs/guides/BRANCH_PROTECTION.md).
#   3. The security team has at least one member who is not on the platform
#      team and is not the author of the pull request.
#   4. Every team is visible (not secret) and has Write access or higher to
#      this repository. GitHub ignores an owner without it, and a line with
#      no valid owner needs no code-owner review, so a security-only line
#      fails open. `gh api repos/{owner}/{repo}/codeowners/errors` must show
#      no errors.
#
# The current maintainer should join @your-org/platform-team (and the security
# team) rather than being named here, so ownership survives one person leaving.
#
# PRECEDENCE: GitHub applies the LAST matching line only, and ONE approval from
# ANY owner on that line satisfies it. A line that lists the platform and the
# security team therefore accepts a platform approval alone. Only a line that
# lists the security team ALONE makes a security approval required. General
# areas come first; more specific paths come LATER so they win. Keep that order
# when editing.

# ── Default ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
* @your-org/platform-team

# ── CI/CD, supply-chain, and security gates ──────────────────────────────────
# The scanners and the pipeline are a security control, so the security team is
# listed alongside platform (either approval satisfies a two-team line).
/.github/                 @your-org/platform-team @your-org/security-team
/scripts/                 @your-org/platform-team
/Makefile                 @your-org/platform-team
/.terraform-docs.yml      @your-org/platform-team
/.tflint.hcl              @your-org/platform-team
/.checkov.yaml            @your-org/platform-team @your-org/security-team

# ── Deployable roots ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/envs/           @your-org/platform-team
/envs/saas/      @your-org/app-platform-team

# ── Modules ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/modules/gcp/        @your-org/platform-team
/modules/aws/        @your-org/platform-team
/modules/supabase/   @your-org/app-platform-team
/modules/vercel/     @your-org/app-platform-team
/modules/saas/       @your-org/app-platform-team

# ── Examples and docs ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/examples/     @your-org/platform-team
/docs/         @your-org/docs-team
SECURITY.md    @your-org/security-team
CHANGELOG.md   @your-org/platform-team

# ── Control-plane and security roots (platform or security) ────────────────
# Listed after the general /envs/ line so they take precedence. The security
# team is listed so it can approve; a platform approval alone also satisfies
# these lines. envs/tfc-admin also wires the policy sets (main.tf), which is not
# a separate file, so it stays a two-team line.
/envs/gcp/bootstrap/      @your-org/platform-team @your-org/security-team
/envs/gcp/organization/   @your-org/platform-team @your-org/security-team
/envs/aws/organization/   @your-org/platform-team @your-org/security-team
/envs/aws/security/       @your-org/platform-team @your-org/security-team
/envs/aws/identity/       @your-org/platform-team @your-org/security-team
/envs/aws/backup/         @your-org/platform-team @your-org/security-team
/envs/tfc-admin/          @your-org/platform-team @your-org/security-team

# ── Security-sensitive modules (platform or security) ──────────────────────
# IAM, governance/guardrails, KMS, break-glass, and the whole AWS security
# baseline. Listed after the general /modules/ lines so they win. The GCP
# deny-policy module is security-only (Guardrails section below).
/modules/gcp/governance/  @your-org/platform-team @your-org/security-team
/modules/gcp/iam/         @your-org/platform-team @your-org/security-team
/modules/gcp/stages/organization/  @your-org/platform-team @your-org/security-team
/modules/gcp/stages/bootstrap/    @your-org/platform-team @your-org/security-team
/modules/aws/governance/  @your-org/platform-team @your-org/security-team
/modules/aws/iam/         @your-org/platform-team @your-org/security-team
/modules/aws/security/    @your-org/platform-team @your-org/security-team
# The AWS stages that wire the SCPs/RCPs, guard alerts, the org trail, the
# security baseline and the backup policy - the AWS twins of the GCP stages above.
/modules/aws/stages/organization/  @your-org/platform-team @your-org/security-team
/modules/aws/stages/security/      @your-org/platform-team @your-org/security-team
/modules/aws/stages/backup/        @your-org/platform-team @your-org/security-team

# ── Consistency gate and the configuration files (platform or security) ──────
# landing-zone.yaml feeds every root (gcp-guardrails included);
# tfc-workspaces.yaml sets per-workspace variables (credential env vars included).
/scripts/check-consistency.sh     @your-org/platform-team @your-org/security-team
/config/landing-zone.yaml    @your-org/platform-team @your-org/security-team
/config/tfc-workspaces.yaml  @your-org/platform-team @your-org/security-team
/config/sandbox/             @your-org/platform-team @your-org/security-team

# ── Guardrails (security team ONLY: a security approval is REQUIRED) ──────────
# Listed last so these lines win over every broader line above. The OPA policy
# sets, the org IAM deny policies (including the committed
# guardrails.auto.tfvars that holds iam_deny_policies), the plan-time execution
# gate and its parser lock, the AWS phase-0 CloudFormation templates (they
# create the management-account roles), this file and the template it is
# rendered from. Also the deny-policy module the guardrails root uses, the TFC
# workspace module tfc-admin builds every workspace with, and the supply-chain
# pins: Renovate, release-please, the tool versions and the pre-commit hooks.
# The security team must have at least one member who is not on the platform
# team.
/policies/                        @your-org/security-team
/envs/gcp/guardrails/             @your-org/security-team
/modules/gcp/stages/guardrails/   @your-org/security-team
/scripts/check-plan-time-exec.py  @your-org/security-team
/.github/requirements/            @your-org/security-team
/.github/CODEOWNERS               @your-org/security-team
/templates/aws/bootstrap/         @your-org/security-team
/templates/CODEOWNERS.tftpl       @your-org/security-team
/modules/gcp/iam/deny-policy/     @your-org/security-team
/modules/tfc/                     @your-org/security-team
/renovate.json                    @your-org/security-team
/release-please-config.json       @your-org/security-team
/.tool-versions                   @your-org/security-team
/.pre-commit-config.yaml          @your-org/security-team
